# ==============================================================================
# Query Name: 02_bruteforce_attacker_ips.spl
# Project: P1 — Splunk SOC Home Lab & Log Analysis
# Purpose: Top brute-force attacker source IP ranking
# Security Use Case: Triage source IPs generating repeated failed logins and brute-force bursts
# ==============================================================================

index=main auth_success=false OR event_type="Multiple Failed Authentication Attempts"
| stats count as failed_attempts by id.orig_h
| where failed_attempts > 5
| sort - failed_attempts

# Expected Interpretation:
# - Identifies high-frequency offending source IP addresses (e.g., 10.0.0.25, 10.0.0.18).
# - Isolates hosts that exceed a threshold of 5 failed attempts, distinguishing targeted
#   brute-force scripts from occasional legitimate user typos.
# - Provides actionable IOCs (Source IPs) for immediate firewall containment.
